WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
In 2009, Quakers in Britain decided
to celebrate same-sex marriages.

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.880
Then the Methodist Church
in Britain in 2021,

3
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:13.760
and in 2022 the Church of Scotland,
for ministers who choose to.

4
00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:17.700
The Church of England still
does not marry same-sex couples.

5
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.620
Yet these churches share the same Bible.

6
00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.710
Its words have not changed.

7
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.240
So if a church's scripture hasn't changed,

8
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.920
how can its teaching on sex change?

9
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:33.350
In this mission, you'll place churches along
a spectrum of views on same-sex relationships.

10
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.840
Then you'll follow British
law from 1967 to 2022,

11
00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.840
and ask what pushes teaching to move.

12
00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:45.980
Your mission: find out how a church's
teaching on sex can change when its scripture

13
00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:47.070
stays the same.
